      <PkeyDataSourceName>PkTaxRate</PkeyDataSourceName>
      <PluralDisplayName>Tax Rates</PluralDisplayName>
      <AddToCache>true</AddToCache>
      <JsonUsesCapital>false</JsonUsesCapital>
      <EnabledCompareValue>false</EnabledCompareValue>
      <VisibleCompareValue>false</VisibleCompareValue>
      <ContextEnabledCompareValue>false</ContextEnabledCompareValue>
      <ContextVisibleCompareValue>false</ContextVisibleCompareValue>
      <CreatePojo>false</CreatePojo>
      <PojoSingleton>false</PojoSingleton>
      <Total>0</Total>
      <Description></Description>
      <Color>#C0FFC0</Color>
      <Bounds>2426,1098,152,300</Bounds>
      <Help><![CDATA[<span style="font-weight:bold">Note:</span>  for a Location that has 
      more than one tax rate, no other Location can share those tax rates.   
      This is because of how Square finds and selects the taxRate(s) for an 
      Item being sold from a Location.  It looks at the Location.taxRates and 
      matches with any of the Item.taxRates, where the Item.taxRates is a list 
      of all of the taxRates for all of the Locations.
    </p>
    <p style="margin-top:0">
      The calc property &quot;isAvailableForLocation&quot; wil make sure that this rule 
      is followed.  
    </p>
    <p style="margin-top:0">
      For example, if the taxRate is 5% for 3 locations, and one of the 
      locations also has a 2% taxRate for certain items, then a new 5% taxRate 
      needs to be created for this location to use by itself.<br>Rule: if a 
      Location has more than one taxRate, then no other Location can use the 
      same same taxRate.<br><br>]]></Help>
      <Flag>true</Flag>
      <Lookup>false</Lookup>
      <DataSourceName>TaxRate</DataSourceName>
      <PluralName>TaxRates</PluralName>
      <Processed>false</Processed>
      <LowerName>taxRate</LowerName>
      <PluralLowerName>taxRates</PluralLowerName>
      <ShortName>txr</ShortName>
      <LocalOnly>false</LocalOnly>
